  "baseline": "75bb92c4",
  "scope": "Exact unchanged Debian ARM64 Chromium, software/headless Wayland at 100 percent scale; ordinary wrapped native textareas",
  "implementation": {
    "provider": "Native hit testing and ordinary responder scrollWheel: dispatch; actual NSScrollView owns line/page, Shift, native preferences, clamping and pixels. No duplicated control algorithms.",
    "transport": "Optional append-only wheel method and separate capability; owner-connection-only operation 35. Existing keyboard capability, viewport structs and protocol layouts unchanged.",
    "chromium": "Original trusted DOM dispatch/cancellation first; actual native widget region in Blink EventHandlerRegistry defeats compositor bypass without dummy JavaScript. Uncancelled native default returns kHandledSystem, avoiding a second engine default.",
    "recovery": "Replay retained engine scroll model into a recreated native object once per authenticated host generation, after text synchronization. Failed native reads do not echo stale viewport state. No input action replay.",
    "backend": "Pointer-frame axis grouping; wheel/value120/discrete normalization and Wayland positive-down Y to native NSEvent Y. Separate private backend build; no installed AppKit or browser rebuild.",
    "feature": "NEXTSPACE_CHROMIUM_WHEEL=1 requires native multiline viewport flags, wheel capability and exact instruction/build guards. Opt-in; not the installed desktop default."
  },
